{"at": "2026-10-14T12:11:35.858675+00:00", "event_id": "01M4X56F1JCFC9876NY2G29ZYQ", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M4X56F1GE5HAWSXBGWSNMAB9", "input_key": "reading_width_default", "mission_id": "01M4X4XGQ92SEMD7FXG9N01JB1", "mission_slug": "reading-width-01M4X4XG", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["52rem", "56rem", "60rem", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "What should the new --dk-width-content default be (issue proposes ~60rem; settle by line-length measurement)?", "recorded_at": "2026-10-14T12:11:35.858675Z", "run_id": "01M4X56F1GE5HAWSXBGWSNMAB9", "state_entered_at": "2026-10-14T12:11:35.856662Z", "step_id": "specify.layout.reading-width-default"}}
{"at": "2026-10-14T12:11:39.495181+00:00", "event_id": "01M4X56JK7185AFVEX9PER9D41", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M4X56JK56BM2QAXP9C3J7JKV", "input_key": "wide_content_behaviour", "mission_id": "01M4X4XGQ92SEMD7FXG9N01JB1", "mission_slug": "reading-width-01M4X4XG", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["Tables only, to the reading pane, capped by a token", "Tables, diagrams and code", "Keep everything scrolling inside the column", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "Which wide blocks grow past the prose column, and how far?", "recorded_at": "2026-10-14T12:11:39.495181Z", "run_id": "01M4X56JK56BM2QAXP9C3J7JKV", "state_entered_at": "2026-10-14T12:11:39.493585Z", "step_id": "specify.layout.wide-content"}}
{"at": "2026-10-14T12:11:48.405885+00:00", "event_id": "01M4X56V9N5155FG69PEDF0B45", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M4X56F1GE5HAWSXBGWSNMAB9", "final_answer": "52rem. Resolved autonomously from the dispatch brief (issue #154 asks to settle the value by measuring line length). Measured: 45rem = 92-101 chars/line, 52rem = 106-117, 60rem = 123-135. At 1440px a sidebar+rail page is pane-limited to 816px, so 51rem+ fills the pane there; 52rem is the smallest value that does, keeping prose as close to the 45-90 char guideline as the goal allows. Tables get extra room separately. The operator can restate 60rem in review; it is a one-token change.", "mission_id": "01M4X4XGQ92SEMD7FXG9N01JB1", "mission_slug": "reading-width-01M4X4XG", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": false, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-10-14T12:11:48.405885Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M4X56F1GE5HAWSXBGWSNMAB9", "state_entered_at": "2026-10-14T12:11:48.400898Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
{"at": "2026-10-14T12:11:51.616689+00:00", "event_id": "01M4X56YE0KTMGY6NF2T6TSXFM", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M4X56JK56BM2QAXP9C3J7JKV", "final_answer": "Tables only: a table that is a direct child of the page body grows past the prose column, centred on it, up to the reading pane (never under the TOC rail) and at most a new --dk-width-wide token, from the 72rem breakpoint up. Diagrams already scale to fit and code blocks scroll by convention; both stay in the column. Resolved autonomously from the brief (issue prefers growth when it does not hurt the TOC rail).", "mission_id": "01M4X4XGQ92SEMD7FXG9N01JB1", "mission_slug": "reading-width-01M4X4XG", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": true, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-10-14T12:11:51.616689Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M4X56JK56BM2QAXP9C3J7JKV", "state_entered_at": "2026-10-14T12:11:51.613431Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
